  "question": {
    "text": "Let the focal chord $P Q$ of the parabola $y^2=4 x$ make an angle of $60^{\\circ}$ with the positive $x$-axis, where P lies in the first quadrant. If the circle, whose one diameter is PS, S being the focus of the parabola, touches the $y$-axis at the point $(0, \\alpha)$, then $5 \\alpha^2$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lJeH8",
      "text": "15",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CxqyA",
      "text": "25",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "L2ZeS",
      "text": "30",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "WXlD3",
      "text": "20",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/IjTwyqnHbVkOCBXtO1yuOjO-qDCMCQJq6X1EofoXZs4.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>$\\tan 60^{\\circ}=\\frac{2 \\mathrm{t}-0}{\\mathrm{t}^2-1}=\\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{t}=\\sqrt{3}$<br/>$\\therefore \\mathrm{P}(3,2 \\sqrt{3})$<br/>Circle :<br/>$(x-1)(x-3)+(y-0)(y-2 \\sqrt{3})=0$<br/>at $x=0$<br/>$\\Rightarrow 3+y^2-2 \\sqrt{3} y=0$<br/>$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{y}=\\sqrt{3}=\\alpha$<br/>$5 \\alpha^2=15$",
    "image": null
  },
